cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Atlas-E2G, please cite the accompanying manuscript
  Atlas-E2G learns transferable promoter responsiveness from endogenous
  enhancer perturbations by Shuran Li, Zhaonan Zou and Shinya Oki.
title: Atlas-E2G
type: software
repository-code: https://github.com/lishuran160-star/Atlas-E2G
url: https://github.com/lishuran160-star/Atlas-E2G
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Shuran
    affiliation: Institute of Resource Development and Analysis, Kumamoto University
  - family-names: Zou
    given-names: Zhaonan
    affiliation: Institute of Resource Development and Analysis, Kumamoto University
  - family-names: Oki
    given-names: Shinya
    affiliation: Institute of Resource Development and Analysis, Kumamoto University
abstract: >-
  Atlas-E2G learns separate enhancer and promoter contributions from public
  ChIP-Atlas binding profiles and endogenous CRISPR perturbations. It ranks
  enhancer-gene candidates and estimates promoter responsiveness. A separately
  fitted public-reference configuration supports gene-name queries without
  query-cell assays. The package includes processed data, model parameters
  and code to reproduce the main manuscript results.
keywords:
  - enhancer-gene prediction
  - promoter responsiveness
  - ChIP-Atlas
  - CRISPR perturbation
license: MIT
